call was placed, but the content — whether it located her and whether it was answered — is not on the record.\n\nBecause the fact that decides this case — arrival and dwell — is carried by nothing but an absent artifact (EV-GPS-00213, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), my confidence is capped at 0.0 under POL-GEN-02(2), far below the 0.70 floor, and POL-NS-09(a) and (e) require escalation. Independently, POL-NS-09(c) requires it: this rider and this driver already have two no-show disputes between them in the trailing 90 days, and both profiles record it.\n\nTwo smaller points. The $6.00 fee reconciles correctly as the greater of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee, so there is no fare-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d). And the anti-farming check does not trip (3 no-show terminations against 107 completed trips, 2.8%), so no escalation arises through that branch and no compensation is withheld on it.\n\nTo the rider: escalation is not a finding against you, and your $6.00 is held rather than collected. To the driver: it is not a finding against you either, and the reviewer will take your account. The reviewer is asked to settle three things: (1) whether the driver in fact arrived at the bay and dwelt there for at least 300 seconds; (2) the pin question, since the bay carries two registered pickup points and no chat record survives to show which entrance was meant, so POL-NS-03(ii) may fall to be considered; and (3) how the loss of the GPS trace and the chat export should be treated, given that it is the platform's own retention that failed."
